cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyOptik in your research, please cite this software."
title: "PyOptik: optical materials, dispersion, and thin films in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Poinsinet de Sivry-Houle"
    given-names: "Martin"
abstract: >
  PyOptik is an open-source Python package for wavelength-dependent optical
  constants, material dispersion, Fresnel interfaces, and coherent thin films.
  It provides access to the RefractiveIndex.INFO material catalog.
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MartinPdeS/PyOptik"
keywords:
  - optics
  - refractive index
  - optical materials
  - dispersion
  - thin films
